    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Calculates safety stock, reorder points, order-up-to levels and EOQ per item from demand history and lead times for a target service level, with a reorder list.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Supply Chain",
    "tags": [
        "safety stock",
        "reorder point",
        "inventory",
        "eoq",
        "service level",
        "supply chain",
        "replenishment",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Sets stock levels from demand history for a target **service level** (the chance of not running out during a replenishment lead time):\n\n| Output | Formula |\n|---|---|\n| Average demand, standard deviation | per period (day, week, month); periods with **no demand count as zero** |\n| **Safety stock** | z x sqrt(L x sd_d² + d² x sd_L²), with z from the service level, L the lead time and sd_L its variability |\n| **Reorder point** | d x L + safety stock |\n| **Order-up-to level** | for periodic review: d x (L + R) + z x sqrt((L + R) x sd_d² + d² x sd_L²) |\n| **EOQ** | sqrt(2 x annual demand x ordering cost / (holding rate x unit cost)), when costs are given |\n| Cover, status, suggested order | from stock on hand: items at or below the reorder point and the quantity to bring them to the order-up-to level |\n\nInput 1 is demand history (item, date, quantity: orders or daily sales lines). Optional input 2 has one row per item with its lead time (in periods), lead-time standard deviation, unit cost, stock on hand and an item-specific service level. Without input 2, one lead time applies to all items.",
